cff-version: 1.2.0

title: >-
  Fairness-Constrained Load-Shedding Optimisation with Cold Load Pickup:
  Ambient Temperature versus Outage Duration as Surge Drivers in a
  Chronically Constrained Grid

abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a study of cold-load-pickup surge drivers in
  rotational load shedding, built on SCADA telemetry from five Iraqi
  governorates (206,040 hourly records, 2020-2024). Contains the
  fairness-constrained multi-scenario MILP, per-governorate BiLSTM demand
  forecasting with LSTM, GRU and XGBoost benchmarks, five model
  configurations across six thermal regimes, solver-gap diagnostics and
  lower bounds, kernel and scenario sensitivity analyses, budget-stability
  re-solves and discomfort-weighting robustness re-solves.

